il Jendoubi"] " of Tunisia 16-12 to win the Olympic gold medal in the men’s 58kg Taekwondo final at Tokyo. The 20-year-old European champion, who was making his Olympic début, launched his attack on Jendoubi from the start of a closely fought contest at the Makuhari Messe, Hall A, in Tokyo. They were tied at 10-10 with seconds left on the clock before Dell’Aquila won with a series of strikes."] "\n\n" [:p {} "At a press conference afterwards, the winner said he was happy with his victory and was now looking forward to having some rest when he returned home to Italy. Jendoubi had caused an upset earlier on the opening day when he beat the world champion and favorite for gold, " [:a {:href "/athletes/145048"} "Jang Jun"] " of the Republic of Korea, in their semi-final bout 25-19. Jang Jun and number five seed Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/146280"} "Mikhail Artamonov"] " went through the repêchage to win bronze medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144220"} "Vito Dell'Aquila"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2504138"} "Mohamed Khalil Jendoubi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUN.png"}] "TUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145048"} "Jang Jun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu